From 9f540368faa8ff0b2845977c71889b580e09f929 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jon <resands@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 22:19:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Compiled VU0 microprograms: vu1_recomp also compiles 4 KB VU0
 images (vu0_*.bin), the runtime runs VCALLMS programs compiled

VU0 microprograms ran on the cycle-modelling interpreter (about 38% of the game thread in slow
PoP scenes). They now go through the same compiled path as VU1:
- PS2X_VU1_CAPTURE also records VU0 images (vu0_<hash>.bin, entries_vu0.txt);
- vu1_recomp compiles vu0_*.bin with the VU0 decoder (no EFU/XGKICK), 4 KB code (branch and
  JR masks) and 4 KB data (qaddr0), and registers them with registerVu0CompiledProgram;
- the runtime looks VU0 programs up in their own registry (by the whole 4 KB image and the
  VU0 code generation); PS2X_VU0_RECOMP=0 turns it off, PS2X_VU0_VERIFY=1 checks every run
  against the interpreter like PS2X_VU1_VERIFY;
- the fast path takes the data size from the unit (Vu1FastCtx::memSize), and VU0 has its own
  norm shadow, verifier shadow and stats (thread_local), since VU0 runs on the EE thread.
